# Bind-Then-Compose Dispatch

Transport shapes, `nest_under`, packet scoping: `consult-routing` § Bind-then-compose split.

## Invariant (one line)

`judgment_closed ∧ mechanical_remainder ⇒ split_dispatch(bind_leg, compose_leg)` —
premium / reasoning models **bind**; **`cursor/composer-2.5`** (default `seat=cursor-sdk`
generate) **implements** nested — ¬ one dispatch doing both.

## Enforced in substrate on the cursor-auto lane (operator bind 2026-08-09)

On the unattended `cursor-auto` lane this is **no longer advisory** —
`services/git_integration_worker/cursor_auto/dispatch_bounds.py` enforces it. Auto
POSTs the cursor-sdk worker directly, so Stargate's `sdk_cost_risk` guard never sees
these binds; `premium_bind` announced premium spend and nothing gated it.

| Bound | Behavior | Check |
|---|---|---|
| **Executor** | `contract=implement` (→ `pure-mechanical`) redirects to `cursor/composer-2.5` — a reasoning model **never** runs the mechanical leg | `frontier.sdk.auto.mechanical_executor_redirected` |
| **Scope** | a `contract:` override no longer waives the empty-scope refusal outside the roaming tier | `frontier.sdk.auto.empty_directive_scope_blocked` |
| **Effort** | values the model card accepts pass; above-card rungs degrade to the highest accepted (`clamp_effort_to_model_card` / `compose_model_knobs`) | admit turn `resolved_effort` |

**Roaming tier** = `composer-2.5`, `composer-2.5-fast`, `grok-4.6`. Everything else —
opus, sonnet, fable, `gpt-5.6-*` — is bounded. `desired_model: auto` resolves *into*
the roaming tier, so the default mechanical path is untouched.

Naming a reasoning model on an implement contract is no longer a violation you can
commit: it is corrected and announced. Redirect ¬ refuse — the work is legitimate,
only the executor was wrong. SOT: `decision:autonomous-dispatch-bounds`.

## When the split is mandatory

Fire **two legs** (or bind in-seat + compose dispatch) when **ANY**:

- Packet / todo carries `files_expected` + `acceptance_criteria` (implement-shaped)
- `contract=implement` or densified spec is the deliverable
- `density_triage=judgment_required` and the arc still has a write/edit step after bind
- Admit emits `sdk_cost_risk` / mechanical `KnobRecommendation` (`dispatch_knob_policy`)
- `executor_override` names Opus/Sonnet/Fable for work that is mechanical after bind

## Two legs (default)

| Leg | Seat / model | Contract | Output |
|---|---|---|---|
| **1 — Bind** | `cdp/opus-5`, `cdp/fable`, `cursor/grok-4.6`, or `cursor/claude-opus-5` (inform-then-proceed) | `light-bounded` | Dense packet, spec, or sidecar: scope, invariants, `files_expected`, `acceptance_criteria` — **no repo writes** unless bind requires a spec file |
| **2 — Compose** | `seat=cursor-sdk` (omit `model=` → Composer) | `implement` or `pure-mechanical` | Edits + verify per packet; poll `poll_hint` |

```python
# Leg 2 — after bind closes (same arc thread)
team_dispatch(
    op="generate",
    seat="cursor-sdk",
    contract="implement",  # or pure-mechanical when packet is fully pinned
    packet_path="tmp/reviews/{slug}-implement.md",  # or source_ref=todo:{slug}
    dispatch_thread_id="{arc-id}",
    nest_under="{parent_dispatch_id}",  # when parent still holds cursor_sdk_gate
)
```

Chained hops (CDP → auto → specialist) **must** `nest_under` the live lease holder
(`cdp-operator-proxy` inv 19 · `operator-proxy-substrate` § Nesting + lease).
¬ fresh top-level contend under an active gate.

## Exempt (single leg OK)

- Trivial/local: ≤ few lines, loci known, self-verifiable (lean-context trivial row)
- **Bind-only** consult: no write intent; answer closes the arc
- Implement packet already dense **before** premium consult — bind leg was a prior turn;
  compose leg only (¬ re-spend Opus on amendments: `lean-context-dispatch-first` non-primary gate)

## Anti-patterns

| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| `cursor/claude-opus-5` + `light-bounded` + implement acceptance in one packet | Opus bind sidecar → nested `cursor-sdk` `contract=implement` |
| `executor_override: cursor/claude-opus-5` on mechanical implement | Omit `model=` on `seat=cursor-sdk` implement (Composer default) |
| Ignore `sdk_cost_risk` at admit | Split or downgrade to Composer before edits |
| Premium model runs quality_gate/pytest loops on known files | Composer leg + lead verify sample |
| Treat the split as guidance the orchestrator may skip when in a hurry | On `cursor-auto` it is substrate; the redirect fires whether or not you meant it |

## Composes with

- `lean-context-dispatch-first` — dispatch-first + non-primary model gate
- `consult-routing` — implement lane, model split, surface gate
- `path-sim` — bundled Q→A→R→implement cascade (compose = Stage-B)
